# ============================================================================
# MAINTENANCE MODE — now controlled dynamically, not by editing this file
# ============================================================================
# Superseded by netlify/edge-functions/maintenance-gate.ts, which checks the
# admin-toggleable `maintenance_mode` flag in the app_settings table on every
# request. Toggle it from Admin → Tools (AdminTools.tsx) — takes effect
# site-wide within ~15 seconds, no redeploy needed.
#
# The static on/off rules that used to live here (requiring a file edit +
# redeploy every time) have been removed for that reason. Everything below
# is still required, permanent infrastructure — keep it regardless of
# whether maintenance mode is currently on or off.
#
# Netlify processes edge functions BEFORE _redirects on every request, so
# maintenance-gate.ts already runs first and decides whether to rewrite to
# /maintenance.html — these rules just make sure a few specific paths are
# never caught by that decision, and are pure passthroughs (no maintenance
# logic lives here anymore).
# ============================================================================

# ── 1. Never redirect Netlify Functions ─────────────────────────────────────
# Webhooks — most importantly payfast-webhook.js — must keep working even
# while the site is in maintenance mode. If a PayFast payment confirmation
# got redirected to the maintenance page instead of reaching the function,
# a customer could be charged without their credits ever being granted.
# Scheduled functions (match-scan-daily, monthly-pro-credits,
# vacancies-refresh-daily) aren't affected by _redirects either way — they
# run on Netlify's internal scheduler, not via a matched HTTP path — but
# this rule is still required for anything triggered by an external call
# (webhooks) or the app's own fetch() calls (deduct-credits, grant-signup-
# credits, admin-*, etc.), all of which DO go through this file.
# (maintenance-gate.ts also exempts this path itself, independently —
# this rule is a second layer of the same protection.)
/.netlify/functions/*   /.netlify/functions/:splat   200

# ── 2. Always allow the hidden bypass page to load ──────────────────────────
# This is what sets the bypass cookie maintenance-gate.ts checks for.
# See maintenance-access.html for the secret key check.
/maintenance-access.html   /maintenance-access.html   200

# ── 3. Always allow the maintenance page's own request to pass through ─────
# (Not strictly required — a self-referential redirect isn't a loop — but
# explicit here so it's obvious this path is intentionally exempt too.)
/maintenance.html   /maintenance.html   200

